    "https://employment.marquette.edu/postings/25437": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant Professor - Psychology",
      "description": "Marquette University | Teaching Assistant Professor - Psychology Skip to Main Content Employment at Marquette Human Resources About Marquette Contact Human Resources Employment at Marquette Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Employee Benefits Diversity & Title IX Human Resources Marquette News Campus Map Visit Marquette Teaching Assistant Professor - Psychology Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number 201104791 Position Title Teaching Assistant Professor - Psychology State WI Employment Status Full Time Position Status Regular If Limited Term (End Date of Assignment, Project, or Grant) Position Type Faculty Job Family Faculty # Hours Per Week Position Overview The Department of Psychology at Marquette University invites applications for a Teaching Assistant Professor position beginning August 2027. The area of expertise is open. The position requires teaching four courses per semester with opportunities to reduce course load by engaging in service, such as academic advising of undergraduate students. Opportunities for summer teaching are also available. To reduce the number of new preps, the courses per semester can include multiple sections of the same course (if available), and the two semesters will entail teaching similar courses. We are particularly interested in candidates with a track-record of teaching that focuses on marginalization with respect to mental health, adaptation, bias, thriving, etc. The successful candidate would teach a range of possible courses at the undergraduate level such as Psychology of Racism, Psychology of Prejudice, Psychology of Religion, Psychology of Gender Roles, and/or Death and Dying. Candidates who can contribute to teaching graduate courses in the Clinical Psychology Ph.D. program would be desirable. Although research is not required for this position, laboratory resources can be made available for individuals who desire to engage in scholarship. Marquette University is a Jesuit, Catholic university with approximately 8,400 undergraduate and 3,300 graduate and professional students across a wide range of programs. We seek candidates who understand and respect the University’s Mission, which is shaped in part by the Apostolic Preferences ( https://www.marquette.edu/mission-ministry/catholic-jesuit-identity.php ). Marquette University is an Equal Opportunity Employer that is committed to diversity and equity for all individuals including age, culture, faith, ethnicity, race, gender, sexual orientation, language, disability, and social class (http://www.marquette.edu/diversity/statement.shtml). The university is located in urban Milwaukee, a large and ethnically diverse city. All applications for this position must be received through Marquette University’s electronic recruiting system. Please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae (CV), and unofficial graduate transcripts. Three letters of reference will be required during the interview stage of the search.Please submit application materials by October 31 for full consideration although review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position can be addressed to the search committee chairperson, Dr. Kimberly D’Anna-Hernandez ( kimberly.danna-hernandez@marquette.edu ) or to the department chairperson Dr. Lucas Torres ( lucas.torres@marquette.edu ). Duties and Responsibilities Responsibilities include teaching courses that contribute to the Diversity and Inclusion content area of our undergraduate curriculum and/or our APA -accredited Ph.D. program in Clinical Psychology, and advising of undergraduate students. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Earned doctorate or a terminal degree. Demonstrated potential for teaching excellence and high quality research. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Abilities ABD may be considered. Department Psychology Posting Date 09/14/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants EOE Statement It is the policy of Marquette University to provide equal employment opportunities ( EEO ) to all employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status or any other applicable federal or state-protected classification. Required Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Teaching Philosophy Unofficial Transcripts References Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). © 2013 Marquette University, \"Be The Difference\" is registered in the U.S. Patent and Trademark Office. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.marquette.edu/postings/25424": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Occupational Therapy",
      "description": "Marquette University | Adjunct Faculty, Occupational Therapy Skip to Main Content Employment at Marquette Human Resources About Marquette Contact Human Resources Employment at Marquette Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Employee Benefits Diversity & Title IX Human Resources Marquette News Campus Map Visit Marquette Adjunct Faculty, Occupational Therapy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number 201104871 Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Occupational Therapy State Employment Status Part Time Position Status Limited Term If Limited Term (End Date of Assignment, Project, or Grant) 05/21/2027 Position Type Faculty Job Family Faculty # Hours Per Week Position Overview The Department of Occupational Therapy in the College of Health Sciences at Marquette University invites applications for an adjunct position in the entry-level Occupational Therapy Doctorate ( OTD ) Program. Rank and salary commensurate with experience. The successful applicant will join an innovative team in the didactic and clinical development and implementation of the OTD program in compliance with the Accreditation Council for Occupational Therapy Education ( ACOTE ) educational standards. Duties and Responsibilities Responsibilities include lab supervision/course instruction, assistance with practicals, direct student teaching. Prior experience in the teaching doctoral students preferred. Must fulfill duties as assigned by the Chair and Program Director of the OT Department and/or the Dean of the College. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Minimum qualifications: an earned doctoral degree from a USDE regionally accredited institution; current Wisconsin licensure as an occupational therapist (or eligibility for licensure) in good standing; current National Board for Certification in Occupational Therapy ( NBCOT ); at least 2 years clinical practice experience as an Occupational Therapist. The successful candidate will promote and demonstrate professional behavior consistent with the standards of the occupational therapy profession and be committed to the core values of a Jesuit university. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Preferred qualifications: documented experience teaching in an occupational therapy education program; evidence of engagement in community-based practice. Department Occupational Therapy Posting Date 09/11/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants EOE Statement It is the policy of Marquette University to provide equal employment opportunities ( EEO ) to all employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status or any other applicable federal or state-protected classification. Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae References Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). © 2013 Marquette University, \"Be The Difference\" is registered in the U.S. Patent and Trademark Office. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
