    "https://employment.marquette.edu/postings/25189": {
      "title": "Director of Advanced Laboratories &amp; Undergraduate Professional Development",
      "description": "Marquette University | Director of Advanced Laboratories &amp; Undergraduate Professional Development Skip to Main Content Employment at Marquette Human Resources About Marquette Contact Human Resources Employment at Marquette Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Employee Benefits Diversity & Title IX Human Resources Marquette News Campus Map Visit Marquette Director of Advanced Laboratories & Undergraduate Professional Development Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. All applications for this position must be received through Marquette University’s electronic recruiting system. Please include a cover letter, CV, unofficial transcripts (both undergrad and grad), a teaching statement, and three (3) letters of recommendation. Letters of reference should come from the referee’s university/professional email account and be sent directly to muchem@marquette.edu. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number 201104809 Position Title Director of Advanced Laboratories & Undergraduate Professional Development State WI Employment Status Full Time Position Status Regular If Limited Term (End Date of Assignment, Project, or Grant) Position Type Faculty Job Family Faculty # Hours Per Week Position Overview The Chemistry department of Marquette University is seeking qualified applicants to direct its upper-division laboratory courses and coordinate professional development opportunities for students interested in the chemical sciences. The candidate will develop and implement the laboratory curriculum of upper-level laboratory courses, working closely with other faculty members. The candidate will also promote the professional development of chemistry and biochemistry majors by facilitating undergraduate research, internship positions, career opportunities, and contacts with local companies and organizations in the chemical field. This is a non-tenure track, nine-month faculty position. Duties and Responsibilities • Develop, test, implement, and assess the laboratory curriculum of these courses, working with faculty members involved in the lecture portions. • Supervise, train, and evaluate TAs assigned to the upper division labs. • Teach both the lecture and laboratory portions of one upper-division course per year. • Maintain instrumentation and chemical inventories. • Facilitate undergraduate research opportunities, including summer undergraduate research fellowships. • Cultivate internship opportunities for Chemistry and Biochemistry majors and serve as contact for companies and organizations looking to hire chemistry and biochemistry majors. • Organize yearly panels with professionals from industry, government, and the non-profit sector. Arrange student visits to chemical companies in the Milwaukee area. • Serve as advisor to CheMU – the organization for undergraduate students interested in Chemistry. • Assist and advise students interested in pursuing graduate and/or professional studies. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities M.S. in Chemistry or related field. Three years of teaching experience or other suitable professional experience. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Ph.D. in Chemistry or related field Experience directing laboratory courses at colleges or universities. Department Chemistry Posting Date 07/14/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants All applications for this position must be received through Marquette University’s electronic recruiting system. Please include a cover letter, CV, unofficial transcripts (both undergrad and grad), a teaching statement, and three (3) letters of recommendation. Letters of reference should come from the referee’s university/professional email account and be sent directly to muchem@marquette.edu. EOE Statement It is the policy of Marquette University to provide equal employment opportunities ( EEO ) to all employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status or any other applicable federal or state-protected classification. Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae References Unofficial Transcripts Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). © 2013 Marquette University, \"Be The Difference\" is registered in the U.S. Patent and Trademark Office. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.marquette.edu/postings/25176": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Accounting (Tenure Track) - Fall 2027",
      "description": "Marquette University | Assistant Professor of Accounting (Tenure Track) - Fall 2027 Skip to Main Content Employment at Marquette Human Resources About Marquette Contact Human Resources Employment at Marquette Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Employee Benefits Diversity & Title IX Human Resources Marquette News Campus Map Visit Marquette Assistant Professor of Accounting (Tenure Track) - Fall 2027 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number 201104793 Position Title Assistant Professor of Accounting (Tenure Track) - Fall 2027 State Wisconsin Employment Status Full Time Position Status Regular If Limited Term (End Date of Assignment, Project, or Grant) Position Type Faculty Job Family Faculty # Hours Per Week 37.5 Position Overview Marquette University invites applications for one tenure-track position beginning Fall 2027 to be filled at the rank of Assistant Professor. Applicants should hold a doctoral degree or be in the final stages of dissertation. Relevant work experience and/or professional certifications are preferred but not required. Scholars with expertise in either archival or experimental methods are encouraged to apply. The normal teaching load is 12 semester hours (6 hours each semester) during the first year and 15 semester hours thereafter. Salary and research support are competitive, including travel funds and guaranteed summer support for at least the first three years. Duties and Responsibilities Teaching either financial accounting or accounting technology at the undergraduate and graduate ( MSA ) levels, conduct high-quality research and engage in service activities. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Earned doctorate or a terminal degree. Demonstrated potential for teaching excellence and high quality research. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Abilities ABD may be considered. Department Accounting Posting Date 07/10/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants EOE Statement It is the policy of Marquette University to provide equal employment opportunities ( EEO ) to all employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status or any other applicable federal or state-protected classification. Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts References Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). © 2013 Marquette University, \"Be The Difference\" is registered in the U.S. Patent and Trademark Office. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
