    "https://employment.marquette.edu/postings/25174": {
      "title": "Schneider Endowed Distinguished Professor- Psychology",
      "description": "Marquette University | Schneider Endowed Distinguished Professor- Psychology Skip to Main Content Employment at Marquette Human Resources About Marquette Contact Human Resources Employment at Marquette Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Employee Benefits Diversity & Title IX Human Resources Marquette News Campus Map Visit Marquette Schneider Endowed Distinguished Professor- Psychology Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number 201104792 Position Title Schneider Endowed Distinguished Professor- Psychology State WI Employment Status Full Time Position Status Regular If Limited Term (End Date of Assignment, Project, or Grant) Position Type Faculty Job Family Faculty # Hours Per Week Position Overview The Department of Psychology at Marquette University invites applications for the Schneider Endowed Distinguished Professor, a position at the advanced Associate or Full Professor level beginning August 2027. The Schneider Endowed Distinguished Professorship was established to advance scholarship and training in a mental health treatment related field and, as such, we are particularly interested in candidates with an established track-record of investigating trauma or addiction. Priority will be given to qualified candidates trained in Clinical Psychology with strong evidence as a scholar, teacher, and mentor, but other qualifications will be considered. The ideal candidate will be able to contribute to the department’s scholarship, commitment to teaching undergraduate and graduate students, and community engagement. Research or scholarship responsibilities include conducting transformative research in trauma or addictions, developing an independent research program with potential for extramural funding, establishing a strong publication record, and research mentorship of undergraduate and graduate students. Teaching responsibilities may include undergraduate and graduate teaching (for our APA -accredited Ph.D. program in Clinical Psychology), and/or clinical supervision of graduate student clinicians in our department clinic, the Center for Psychological Services. The ideal candidate will be licensed or license eligible in Wisconsin. Marquette University is a Jesuit, Catholic university with approximately 8,400 undergraduate and 3,300 graduate and professional students across a wide range of programs. We seek candidates who understand and respect the University’s Mission Statement, which can be found at http://www.marquette.edu/about/mission.shtml . Marquette University is an Equal Opportunity Employer that is committed to diversity and equity for all individuals including age, culture, faith, ethnicity, race, gender, sexual orientation, language, disability, and social class (http://www.marquette.edu/diversity/statement.shtml). The university is located in urban Milwaukee, a large and ethnically diverse city. All applications for this position must be received through Marquette University’s electronic recruiting system. Please submit a cover letter, curriculum vita (CV), research and teaching statements, and reprints (optional) to be considered for the position. Candidates will be asked to submit three letters of reference and transcripts in the later stages of the interview process. Please submit application materials by September 18th for full consideration although review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position can be addressed to the department chairperson Dr. Lucas Torres (lucas.torres@marquette.edu). Duties and Responsibilities Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Ph.D. with seven-ten years of college teaching experience. Distinguished teaching and scholarship with established reputation among scholars commensurate with the appointment to a senior rank with tenure. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Department Psychology Posting Date 07/10/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants EOE Statement It is the policy of Marquette University to provide equal employment opportunities ( EEO ) to all employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status or any other applicable federal or state-protected classification. Required Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Teaching Philosophy Research Statement Optional Documents Writing Sample Unofficial Transcripts References Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). © 2013 Marquette University, \"Be The Difference\" is registered in the U.S. Patent and Trademark Office. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.marquette.edu/postings/25173": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Practice, Finance, Full-Time, Fall 2027",
      "description": "Marquette University | Assistant Professor of Practice, Finance, Full-Time, Fall 2027 Skip to Main Content Employment at Marquette Human Resources About Marquette Contact Human Resources Employment at Marquette Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Employee Benefits Diversity & Title IX Human Resources Marquette News Campus Map Visit Marquette Assistant Professor of Practice, Finance, Full-Time, Fall 2027 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number 201104778 Position Title Assistant Professor of Practice, Finance, Full-Time, Fall 2027 State Wisconsin Employment Status Full Time Position Status Regular If Limited Term (End Date of Assignment, Project, or Grant) Position Type Faculty Job Family Faculty # Hours Per Week 37.5 Position Overview Marquette University’s Department of Finance invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure track Assistant Professor of Practice. This position supports the College of Business Administration’s newly launched AI in Business major and contributes to the Finance Department’s growing emphasis on the intersection of artificial intelligence, data-driven decision-making, and financial practice. The successful candidate will be an innovative educator with applied expertise in AI and finance, committed to preparing students for careers in a rapidly evolving industry. Duties and Responsibilities The candidate will teach courses in AI in Finance and related areas, with a standard load of 24 credit hours per academic year. A reduced load of 18 credit hours per year may be considered for candidates who hold a Ph.D. or terminal degree and maintain an active research agenda. Responsibilities include: • Teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in AI in Finance, fintech, data analytics for finance, and related subjects • Develop and update course materials to reflect current tools, industry practices, and emerging applications of AI in financial services • Contribute to the College’s AI in Business major through curriculum design, cross-departmental collaboration, and advising • Mentor and advise students on academic and career development • Participate in departmental, college, and university service, including committee work, program assessment, and shared governance • Pursue scholarly or applied research in AI and finance (a Ph.D. or terminal degree plus an active research agenda is required for 18-credit load consideration) Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Master’s degree in Finance, Financial Engineering, Data Science, or a closely related field from an AACSB -accredited institution Demonstrated experience applying artificial intelligence or machine learning tools in a finance or business context Evidence of effective college-level teaching or strong potential for teaching excellence Strong communication skills and a commitment to student engagement and learning Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Ph.D. in Finance, Financial Economics, Data Science, or a related field (strongly preferred) Industry experience in fintech, quantitative finance, algorithmic trading, or AI-driven financial applications Experience developing or teaching courses that integrate Python, machine learning, or AI tools in a finance curriculum Familiarity with AI in Business program design at the undergraduate or graduate level Active research agenda in AI, fintech, or quantitative finance Certifications in relevant areas such as Python for Data Science, Machine Learning, or CFA Department Finance (Business Admin.) Posting Date 07/10/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants EOE Statement It is the policy of Marquette University to provide equal employment opportunities ( EEO ) to all employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status or any other applicable federal or state-protected classification. Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Curriculum Vitae References Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). © 2013 Marquette University, \"Be The Difference\" is registered in the U.S. Patent and Trademark Office. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.marquette.edu/postings/25172": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Practice/Academic Coordinator - Financial Planning Program - Full Time, Fall 2027",
      "description": "Marquette University | Assistant Professor of Practice/Academic Coordinator - Financial Planning Program - Full Time, Fall 2027 Skip to Main Content Employment at Marquette Human Resources About Marquette Contact Human Resources Employment at Marquette Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Employee Benefits Diversity & Title IX Human Resources Marquette News Campus Map Visit Marquette Assistant Professor of Practice/Academic Coordinator - Financial Planning Program - Full Time, Fall 2027 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number 201104779 Position Title Assistant Professor of Practice/Academic Coordinator - Financial Planning Program - Full Time, Fall 2027 State Wisconsin Employment Status Full Time Position Status Regular If Limited Term (End Date of Assignment, Project, or Grant) Position Type Faculty Job Family Faculty # Hours Per Week 37.5 Position Overview Marquette University’s Department of Finance invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure track Assistant Professor of Practice to serve as Academic Coordinator of the CFP Board Registered financial planning concentration. This position provides academic leadership for the financial planning program while contributing to the Finance Department’s commitment to experiential learning and industry engagement. The successful candidate will be an accomplished educator with expertise in financial planning, dedicated to student success and the advancement of the financial planning profession. Duties and Responsibilities The standard teaching load is 21 credit hours per academic year for candidates without a terminal degree. A reduced load of 18 credit hours per academic year will be considered for candidates who hold a terminal degree, or who are ABDs in advanced dissertation stages, and maintain an active research agenda. This is a 9-month position with opportunities for summer teaching for overload compensation. Primary responsibilities center on teaching, student advising, and curriculum design, including: Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in financial planning, including retirement planning, estate planning, tax planning, investment planning, and risk management Advise and mentor financial planning students on academic progress, course planning, and career pathways in the financial planning profession Design, develop, and continuously update curriculum for the financial planning concentration to ensure alignment with CFP Board education requirements and evolving industry standards Assess student learning outcomes and contribute to program-level assessment and accreditation efforts As Academic Coordinator of the financial planning program, the position carries additional responsibilities including: Oversee day-to-day administration of the CFP Board Registered financial planning concentration, ensuring ongoing compliance with CFP Board education requirements Coordinate with faculty and administration on course scheduling and program continuous improvement Participate in departmental, college, and university committees, events, and student support activities (e.g., learning assessment, internship and career liaison activities, prospective student visits) Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Master’s degree in Financial Planning, Finance, or a closely related field from an AACSB -accredited institution CFP® certification in good standing Evidence of effective college-level teaching or strong potential for teaching excellence Strong commitment to student engagement, advising, and professional development Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Terminal degree in Financial Planning, Finance, or a closely related field (strongly preferred); ABDs in advanced dissertation stages will be considered Experience coordinating or administering a CFP Board Registered academic program Industry experience as a practicing CFP® professional Experience developing financial planning curriculum at the undergraduate or graduate level Active research agenda in financial planning, personal finance, or retirement income planning Department Finance (Business Admin.) Posting Date 07/10/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants EOE Statement It is the policy of Marquette University to provide equal employment opportunities ( EEO ) to all employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status or any other applicable federal or state-protected classification. Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Curriculum Vitae References Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). © 2013 Marquette University, \"Be The Difference\" is registered in the U.S. Patent and Trademark Office. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
