      "description": "Marquette University | Adjunct Instructor - Nurse Anesthesia Educational Program Skip to Main Content Employment at Marquette Human Resources About Marquette Contact Human Resources Employment at Marquette Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Employee Benefits Diversity & Title IX Human Resources Marquette News Campus Map Visit Marquette Adjunct Instructor - Nurse Anesthesia Educational Program Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. All applications for this position must be received through Marquette University’s electronic recruiting system. Upload: 1. CV/Resume 2. Unofficial Transcripts for All Degrees Earned under Unofficial Transcripts 1, Unofficial Transcripts 2, and Unofficial Transcripts 3. 3. Two (2) letters of recommendation under Other Document 1 and Other Document 2. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number 201104789 Position Title Adjunct Instructor - Nurse Anesthesia Educational Program State Wisconsin Employment Status Part Time Position Status Limited Term If Limited Term (End Date of Assignment, Project, or Grant) 06/30/2027 Position Type Faculty Job Family Faculty # Hours Per Week Varied based on courses/sections taught Position Overview The College of Nursing, Nurse Anesthesia Educational Program invites candidates withclassroom or clinical expertise and strong teaching skills to submit applications for a nursinginstructor position. The position requires excellence in teaching and strong communication andcollaboration skills. This faculty role includes assessment, implementation, coordination andevaluation of course curriculum; development, implementation and coordination of learningresources; continual monitoring of participant progress; and collaboration with otherstakeholders, disciplines and departments internal and external to Marquette University. Inaddition, faculty will also promote the values, mission and vision of Marquette University. Duties and Responsibilities Commitment to continued development of excellence in teaching and service.Ability to direct and lead students effectively, communicating with faculty andadministration.Provide leadership in improving and sustaining the quality and effectiveness of thecurriculum.Provide direct supervision of nursing students in clinical sites or classroom settings. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Masters Degree required or substantial progress toward the terminal degree. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Online teaching experience highly desirable for didactic instruction. Doctorial degree preferred. Department College of Nursing Posting Date 06/24/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants All applications for this position must be received through Marquette University’s electronic recruiting system. Upload: 1. CV/Resume 2. Unofficial Transcripts for All Degrees Earned under Unofficial Transcripts 1, Unofficial Transcripts 2, and Unofficial Transcripts 3. 3. Two (2) letters of recommendation under Other Document 1 and Other Document 2. EOE Statement It is the policy of Marquette University to provide equal employment opportunities ( EEO ) to all employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status or any other applicable federal or state-protected classification. Required Documents Required Documents Resume Unofficial Transcripts Unofficial Transcripts 2 Unofficial Transcripts 3 Other 