    "https://employment.marquette.edu/postings/24534": {
      "title": "Part-Time Nursing Instructor - Milwaukee or Pleasant Prairie Campus",
      "description": "Marquette University | Part-Time Nursing Instructor - Milwaukee or Pleasant Prairie Campus Skip to Main Content Employment at Marquette Human Resources About Marquette Contact Human Resources Employment at Marquette Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Employee Benefits Diversity & Title IX Human Resources Marquette News Campus Map Visit Marquette Part-Time Nursing Instructor - Milwaukee or Pleasant Prairie Campus Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. All applications for this position must be received through Marquette University’s electronic recruiting system. Upload: 1. Resume 2. Unofficial Transcripts for All Degrees Earned 3. Two (2) letters of recommendation under Other Document 1 and Other Document 2. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number 201104683 Position Title Part-Time Nursing Instructor - Milwaukee or Pleasant Prairie Campus State WISCONSIN Employment Status Part Time Position Status Limited Term If Limited Term (End Date of Assignment, Project, or Grant) 05/18/2027 Position Type Faculty Job Family Faculty # Hours Per Week Position Overview The College of Nursing invites candidates with classroom or clinical expertise and strong teaching skills to submit applications for a part-time nursing instructor position. The position requires excellence in teaching and strong communication and collaboration skills. This faculty role includes assessment, implementation, coordination and evaluation of course curriculum; development, implementation and coordinator of learning resources; continual monitoring of participant progress; and collaboration with other stakeholders, disciplines and departments internal and external to Marquette University. In addition, faculty will also promote the values, mission and vision of Marquette University. Duties and Responsibilities Commitment to continued development of excellence in teaching and service. Ability to direct and lead students effectively, communicating with faculty and administration. Provide leadership in improving and sustaining the quality and effectiveness of the curriculum. Provide direct supervision of nursing students in clinical sites or classroom settings. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Master’s degree in nursing, eligibility for Wisconsin licensure. Demonstrates potential forteaching excellence and service. The candidate should be forward thinking and committed to preparing the next generation of nurses for excellence in practice. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Previous teaching experience in nursing preferred. Department College of Nursing Posting Date 03/06/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants All applications for this position must be received through Marquette University’s electronic recruiting system. Upload: 1. Resume 2. Unofficial Transcripts for All Degrees Earned 3. Two (2) letters of recommendation under Other Document 1 and Other Document 2. EOE Statement It is the policy of Marquette University to provide equal employment opportunities ( EEO ) to all employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status or any other applicable federal or state-protected classification. Required Documents Required Documents Resume Unofficial Transcripts Other Document 1 Other Document 2 Optional Documents Unofficial Transcripts 2 Unofficial Transcripts 3 Posting Specific Questions Required