    "https://employment.marquette.edu/postings/24504": {
      "title": "Adjunct Assistant Professor - General Practice Residency",
      "description": "Marquette University | Adjunct Assistant Professor - General Practice Residency Skip to Main Content Employment at Marquette Human Resources About Marquette Contact Human Resources Employment at Marquette Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Employee Benefits Diversity & Title IX Human Resources Marquette News Campus Map Visit Marquette Adjunct Assistant Professor - General Practice Residency Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number 201104672 Position Title Adjunct Assistant Professor - General Practice Residency State WI Employment Status Part Time Position Status Limited Term If Limited Term (End Date of Assignment, Project, or Grant) 06/30/2026 Position Type Faculty Job Family Faculty # Hours Per Week 22.5 Position Overview Marquette University School of Dentistry, in association with a local affiliated hospital, seeks a part-time faculty member for its developing Advanced Dental Education General Practice Residency ( GPR ) certificate program. We are looking to fill three days per week, with a minimum of one full day per week. Faculty will join our innovative, growing team to provide the highest standard of comprehensive dental care services with resident teaching, mentoring, curriculum planning and effective supervision inside of our newly renovated clinic space. You will work with high-quality residents in our state-of-the-art clinic with collaborative and engaged colleagues across the healthcare spectrum. Duties and Responsibilities 1. Along with other program faculty, supervise and mentor residents in the Comprehensive Care Clinic within the School of Dentistry. Affiliated hospital privileges are not required. 2. Provide clinical instruction, assistance in teaching and oversight of resident care of patients. 3. Consult and work closely with medical professionals while leading a dental clinic of dental hygiene professionals and auxiliary dental and office staff. 4. Participate in professional and clinical skill development activities with optional continuing education activities at discounted faculty rates. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Qualified applicants must have a DMD / DDS degree from a US or Canadian dental school recognized by the ADA Commission on Dental Accreditation. Applicants must hold or be eligible for a full Wisconsin dental license without restrictions. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Successful completion of either the CODA accredited 1) General Practice Residency ( GPR ) Program or 2) Advanced Education in General Dentistry ( AEGD ) program is preferred but not required Experience and strong interest in dental resident training. Experience or an interest in providing clinical care and instruction in the treatment of patients with medically complex conditions. Department Dental School Posting Date 02/26/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants EOE Statement It is the policy of Marquette University to provide equal employment opportunities ( EEO ) to all employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status or any other applicable federal or state-protected classification. Required Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you have a current Wisconsin dental license? (Open Ended Question) Have you successfully completed either a CODA accredited 1) General Practice Residency (GPR) program or 2) Advanced Education in General Dentistry (AEGD) program? Yes No © 2013 Marquette University, \"Be The Difference\" is registered in the U.S. Patent and Trademark Office. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.marquette.edu/postings/24368": {
      "title": "Part Time Dental Faculty Position- Adjunct Assistant/Associate Professor - Pediatric Dentistry",
      "description": "Marquette University | Part Time Dental Faculty Position- Adjunct Assistant/Associate Professor - Pediatric Dentistry Skip to Main Content Employment at Marquette Human Resources About Marquette Contact Human Resources Employment at Marquette Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Employee Benefits Diversity & Title IX Human Resources Marquette News Campus Map Visit Marquette Part Time Dental Faculty Position- Adjunct Assistant/Associate Professor - Pediatric Dentistry Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number 201104104 Position Title Part Time Dental Faculty Position- Adjunct Assistant/Associate Professor - Pediatric Dentistry State WI Employment Status Part Time Position Status Limited Term If Limited Term (End Date of Assignment, Project, or Grant) Position Type Faculty Job Family Faculty # Hours Per Week 7.5 Position Overview Marquette University School of Dentistry (MUSoD) seeks qualified candidates for a part time faculty position in pediatric dentistry at the school’s main campus in Milwaukee, WI. Minimum weekly commitment is one full day or two half days per week. As Wisconsin’s only dental school, MUSoD is answering the call to meet workforce needs, increase access to oral health care for underserved patients, and advance dental education in Wisconsin. MUSoD serves the community on its main campus in Milwaukee and in outreach clinics across the State of Wisconsin. Duties and Responsibilities Responsibilities include clinical and simulation lab instruction of dental students. Expectations include full participation in all aspects of clinical, nonsurgical pediatric dental care in the clinical and simulation lab settings. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Qualified applicants must have: DMD / DDS degree from a US or Canadian dental school recognized by the ADA Commission on Dental Accreditation. Completed a Pediatric Dentistry Residency Program accredited by the ADA Commission on Dental Accreditation A current, valid license to practice dentistry in the State of Wisconsin. Current CPR certification. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Five years of dental experience focused primarily on pediatrics. Department Dental School Posting Date 02/03/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants EOE Statement It is the policy of Marquette University to provide equal employment opportunities ( EEO ) to all employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status or any other applicable federal or state-protected classification. Required Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Where do you currently hold a valid dental license? (Open Ended Question) Do you currently have a Wisconsin Dental License? Yes No How many days are you available to teach? 1 day 2 days 3 days When would you be available to start? (Open Ended Question) © 2013 Marquette University, \"Be The Difference\" is registered in the U.S. Patent and Trademark Office. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
